  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "Corda is an open-source permissioned distributed ledger platform developed by R3 and purpose-built for regulated industries, where transaction data is shared exclusively between the counterparties involved rather than broadcast to all network participants. Unlike public blockchains, Corda structures its ledger as a directed acyclic graph of Unspent Transaction Outputs (UTXOs) called states, which are consumed and produced by atomic transactions validated by both smart contract code and legal prose. A notary cluster provides consensus on transaction uniqueness, preventing double-spend without revealing transaction details to uninvolved parties, making Corda particularly suited to financial services, trade finance, and healthcare interoperability scenarios.",
